  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class Sui-Generis (HMO-house in multiple occupation) including single storey rear/side extension, rear dormer with outrigger dormer and front rooflights, acoustic entrance canopy and acoustic fence with associated amenity, cycle and refuse storage.\r\r",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, based on its proposed occupation capacity and the ground coverage of proposed ground floor extensions, bin storage and cycle storage; would result in an overdevelopment and over-intensive use of the site as evidenced by the development's excessive quantum of bin storage within a confined front forecourt and provision of an insufficiently sized and poorly configured communal rear garden. The proposed bin storage configuration would unduly detract from the standard of visual amenity provided along the street scene, and the resulting communal rear garden would appear uncharacteristically small in context with surrounding rear gardens. The proposal would therefore be contrary to Policies; D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document (2014) as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed acoustic canopy and associated fencing to the front of the building, by reason of their height, prominence and uncharacteristic presence along the road, would appear as incongruous and discordant additions to the host building and would appear unduly at odds with the established pattern of built form and building frontages visible along the street scene. The proposal would therefore be contrary to Policies; D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010), DMD 6, DMD 8 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document (2014) as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of Bedroom 2's inadequate width and the development's provision of an inadequately sized and poorly configured external communal amenity space would give rise to substandard and inappropriate accommodation, incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers. The development is thereby contrary to Policies; D3 and D6 of the London Plan, CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, DMD 8 and DMD 9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2024)."
  ],
